    <!-- Battery Guide Dialog -->
    <string name="battery_guide_title">Battery Optimization Guide</string>
    <string name="battery_guide_body">Some OEM Android skins aggressively pause background tasks. To make sure cloned messaging or email apps deliver notifications reliably:\n\n1. Open System Battery Settings below.\n2. Locate CloneX in the app list.\n3. Choose \"Unrestricted\" or \"Don\'t optimize\".\n\nCloneX only keeps active clones running when needed.</string>
    <string name="battery_open_system">Open Battery Settings</string>

    <!-- About / FAQ / Privacy Policy -->
    <string name="about_title">About &amp; Help</string>
    <string name="about_tab_overview">About</string>
    <string name="about_tab_faq">FAQ</string>
    <string name="about_tab_privacy">Privacy Policy</string>
    <string name="about_description">CloneX lets you organize and run multiple isolated instances of your installed apps on Android. Every clone maintains its own UUID, sandboxed storage directory, notification controls, and optional security lock.</string>
    <string name="about_engine_note">Cloning Engine Status: Modular CloneEngine architecture ready for local sandbox &amp; virtualization backend integration.</string>

    <string name="faq_q1">How does each clone stay separate?</string>
    <string name="faq_a1">Every clone receives a unique UUID and an isolated storage directory (data and cache) so logins, preferences, and temporary files never collide with the original app or other clones.</string>
    <string name="faq_q2">Why do banking or payment apps show a warning?</string>
    <string name="faq_a2">Financial, UPI/wallet, and DRM streaming apps enforce strict signature and Play Integrity checks for security. They may refuse to open inside virtualized environments.</string>
    <string name="faq_q3">Does CloneX upload my data to any server?</string>
    <string name="faq_a3">No. CloneX works 100% offline on your device. Your clone list, settings, and app data never leave your phone.</string>
    <string name="faq_q4">How do I back up my clone configurations?</string>
    <string name="faq_a4">Go to Settings → Export Clones Backup (JSON) to save your clone metadata locally using Android\'s file picker, and import it anytime.</string>
    <string name="faq_q5">Why can\'t I clone CloneX itself?</string>
    <string name="faq_a5">Self-cloning can cause recursive sandbox loops and conflicting lock states, so CloneX prevents cloning its own package.</string>

    <string name="privacy_policy_title">CloneX Privacy Policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_policy_body">Effective Date: November 2026\n\n1. Zero Data Collection\nCloneX does not collect, transmit, sell, or share any personal data, installed app lists, usage logs, or clone contents with external servers.\n\n2. Local-Only Storage\nAll clone metadata is stored locally in an on-device Room SQLite database. Preferences and lock settings are stored in Jetpack DataStore. Isolated directories reside within your device\'s private app storage.\n\n3. Minimal Permissions\n• Installed Apps Query: Used strictly on-device via standard launcher intent queries to list apps you can clone.\n• Notifications (Android 13+): Requested only after an explanation screen if you enable clone notifications.\n• Boot Completed: Used only if you enable auto-start clones on boot.\n\n4. Full User Control\nYou can clear cache, wipe clone data, export backups, or reset the entire application at any time from Settings.</string>

